[User] Are there Go libraries for parsing OpenDSS and GeoJSON instead of doing it manually?

[Claude] For GeoJSON output: yes, github.com/paulmach/orb is the standard Go geospatial library and would replace the struct definitions and json.RawMessage gymnastics. For OpenDSS DSS format: effectively no — Python has opendssdirect.py but it wraps the full simulation engine via ctypes, not a text parser; no Go equivalent exists. The DSS tokenization logic would need to be hand-written either way. Noted that the assessment says "no external dependencies required" but flagging paulmach/orb in the PR as a production recommendation would read well to reviewers.

